      "versionNonce": 465576323,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785734007617,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Stands for inversion of control .\n\n2. It is a software design principle in which the control of \ncreating objects and managing their dependencies \nis transferred from the programmer to the framework .\n\n3. IOC container is component in spring which implements the \nIOC pattern and perform many responsibilities so that \nprogrammer can focus on buisness logics .\n\n4. Spring IOC container is the core component or heart of \nspring framework .\n\n5. The most important responsibilities of spring framework \nare :\n\n--> Instantiate  the spring bean object .\n\n--> Dependency injection in spring beans .\n\n--> Manage the spring bean life-cycle .\n\n--> destroy the spring bean objects .\n\n\n\nWhat is spring bean ?\n===================\n\nIn spring , any java object which is created or managed by \nIOC is called spring bean .\n\n\nTypes of IOC container \n======================\n\nThere are 2 types of IOC container\n\n1. BeanFactory\n\n--> It is an interface .\n--> available in package org.springframework.beans.factory.\n--> But is old or outdated container.\n\n2. ApplicationContainer\n\n--> It is also an interface .\n--> It inherits from the bean factory .\n--> It is available in package org.springframework.container .\n--> ApplicationContext is the new and modern container .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Stands for inversion of control .\n\n2. It is a software design principle in which the control of \ncreating objects and managing their dependencies \nis transferred from the programmer to the framework .\n\n3. IOC container is component in spring which implements the \nIOC pattern and perform many responsibilities so that \nprogrammer can focus on buisness logics .\n\n4. Spring IOC container is the core component or heart of \nspring framework .\n\n5. The most important responsibilities of spring framework \nare :\n\n--> Instantiate  the spring bean object .\n\n--> Dependency injection in spring beans .\n\n--> Manage the spring bean life-cycle .\n\n--> destroy the spring bean objects .\n\n\n\nWhat is spring bean ?\n===================\n\nIn spring , any java object which is created or managed by \nIOC is called spring bean .\n\n\nTypes of IOC container \n======================\n\nThere are 2 types of IOC container\n\n1. BeanFactory\n\n--> It is an interface .\n--> available in package org.springframework.beans.factory.\n--> But is old or outdated container.\n\n2. ApplicationContainer\n\n--> It is also an interface .\n--> It inherits from the bean factory .\n--> It is available in package org.springframework.container .\n--> ApplicationContext is the new and modern container .",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "B2w1HbCtnHw7iHuwimryr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 251,
